course: dictionary
lesson: 7796
title: Quantity: how much or how many
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A quantity is an amount of something, or how many of it there are. Quantity is a noun, so you can say a quantity, or quantities in the plural. Ask yourself: is this about how much or how many? Then you have found the quantity.
explain: In the lesson sentence, «4 chairs at 136 dollars each cost 136 × 4 = 544 dollars», the quantity is 4, because it is how many chairs there are. The price is 136, and the cost is the price times the quantity.
explain: Quantity also works with words like «large quantities» or «a small quantity». Large quantities means a lot. In «quality, not quantity», the writer says good things matter more than how many there are.
fact: A quantity is an amount or a number of something: how many or how much.
fact: «In quantity» or «large quantities» means a lot of something.
fact: In maths and science, a quantity is anything that can be measured or counted, like length, time or mass.
fact: In the old text «Do not use dishonest standards when measuring length, weight or quantity» (Leviticus 19:35), quantity means how much of something you are measuring.
fact: Toad «found a certain quantity of egg-shells» in a messy kitchen, so here quantity means an amount.
exercise: In «4 chairs at 136 dollars each», what is the quantity? | *4 | dollars | 136 | 544
exercise: Toad «found a certain quantity of egg-shells» at breakfast. What does quantity mean here? | *An amount of them | A kind of breakfast | A broken dish | A spoon
exercise: Which phrase means a lot of something? | Small quantity | Length | *Large quantities | Quality
test: In «quality and quantity», what does quantity mean? | A shopping list | *How much or how many | Length | Good or bad
test: Which of these is a quantity that can be measured? | Kindness | Laughter | *Mass | Friendship
exam: The shop sold a large quantity of apples in one day. What does large quantity mean? | The shop's name | *A lot of apples | A few apples | A low price
